Test 1: Response time - we measure the path from the radar frame capture to the LED turning on and CAN transmission speed. We run at least 50 trials with the object at different 
positions in range of the detection and every trial will have 100 ms or less. 

Test 2: Distance and Accuracy - For distance, a target moves towards the radar from several angles and stops at a five foot line and the program prints the radar’s distance over 
UART to a command window. For accuracy, a log of 10 trials and calculate the percent error for each, and all of them must have a +/- 5% .   

Test 3: False Alarm Rate - With the field cleared of any moving objects, the radar runs for 2 hours while the firmware logs every detections and the LED must activate over UART 
and the test would only pass if the logs show zero detections for the full 2 hours.
 
